# Bash prompt for a command an ask rule matches: "don't ask again" would
# not be honoured (the ask rule still asks), so the option is left out,
# the rest move up a number (Yes / switch to auto mode / No) and its "a"
# shortcut does nothing (permission.Request.Grantable).
@faux testdata/faux/qa/permissions-bash-dontask-hidden.yaml
@setup mkdir -p .claude && printf '{"permissions":{"ask":["Bash(npm test *)"]}}\n' > .claude/settings.json

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE run the upload tests
KEY enter
WAITFOR /approval needed/ 20
SHOT hidden-prompt
EXPECT /npm test -- upload/
EXPECT_NOT /ask again/
EXPECT /2  Yes, and switch to auto mode/
EXPECT /3  No/
EXPECT /press 1, 2 or 3/
KEY a
SHOT after-a
EXPECT /approval needed/
KEY 1
WAITFOR /Ran it once under the ask rule/ 20
SHOT approved-once
EXPECT_NOT /approval needed/
RUN test ! -e .claude/settings.local.json
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
